                <pb facs="0785" n="779" sameAs="frus:frus1942v03/pg779"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.9466A/2: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Huddle</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-02-17T20:00:00-04:00">February 17,
                            1942—8 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>469. Your 460, February 9, 1 p.m. For Tittmann. It is apparent to us that one of
                    the principal objectives which the Japanese hope to accomplish by the
                    establishment of a mission to the Holy See is to influence Catholic sentiment,
                    particularly in the American Republics and to some extent in China and the
                    Philippines.</p>
                <p>In your conversations with Vatican officials you may wish to bring this to their
                    attention.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
